    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in GCA (tocilizumab):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " IL-6 receptor antagonist; consider when starting corticosteroids: allows an accelerated steroid taper and ↓steroid exposure; higher rates of sustained remission once steroids stop; optimal duration not determined; caution w Hx of diverticulitis (diverticular perforation)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) dose, giant cell arteritis (GCA):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " IV 6 mg per kg every 4 wks w tapering course of glucocorticoids. SC: 162 mg once weekly w tapering course of glucocorticoids; 162 mg once every other wk may be prescribed based on clinical considerations."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↑ risk of serious infections that may lead to hospitalization or death; most pts were taking concomitant immunosuppressants such as methotrexate or corticosteroids. Test for latent TB b4 ACTEMRA use and during therapy (except pts w COVID-19); start treatment for latent infection prior to ACTEMRA use."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " known hypersensitivity to ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) GI perforation:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " GI perforation reported, primarily as complications of diverticulitis; use w caution in pts who may be at ↑ risk; promptly evaluate fever, new onset abdominal Sx, and a change in bowel habits for early identification."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) hepatotoxicity:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Obtain liver test panel (ALT, AST, alkaline phosphatase, total bilirubin) b4 ACTEMRA and every 4 to 8 wks for the first 6 mo, then every 3 mo; ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA or SSc-ILD pts w ALT or AST > 1.5× ULN; discontinue if ALT or AST > 5× ULN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) lab monitoring:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA and SSc-ILD pts w ANC less than 2000 per mm3; if ANC less than 500 per mm3 treatment is not recommended. ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA and SSc-ILD pts w platelets below 100,000 per mm3; if platelets less than 50,000 per mm3 treatment is not recommended. Assess lipid parameters approximately 4 to 8 wks following initiation of ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) live vaccines:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ use of live vaccines concurrently w ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) CYP450 interaction:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Inhibition of IL-6 signaling in RA pts treated w tocilizumab may restore CYP450 activities to higher levels than in the absence of tocilizumab, leading to ↑ metabolism of CYP450 substrate drugs. On initiation or discontinuation of ACTEMRA, perform therapeutic monitoring of effect (e.g., warfarin) or drug concentration (e.g., cyclosporine or theophylline) and adjust the dose as needed."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
